-- ===== supplementary case S7: an employee who is neither a citizen nor a permanent resident
-- The independent author expected "not covered", from the BRIEF's scope sentence ("an employee who is a citizen or a permanent resident"); that sentence was loose, not the Act.
-- Central Provident Fund (Exemption) Order 2018 para 3: "An employer is exempt from paying any contribution to the Fund under section 7 of the Act in respect of wages
-- payable to an employee who is not a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore." Nothing is contributed, so nothing is recovered from the employee: CPF 0.
-- Income tax is the ordinary one (a foreign employee can be resident for tax): wages 60,000; earned income relief 1,000; chargeable 59,000; tax 550 on the first 40,000
-- and 7% of 19,000 = 1,330, 1,880; net 60,000 - 1,880 = 58,120. The expectation was changed from "not covered" to these after the Order was read (2026-11-24), and the BRIEF now says so.
#ASSERT `tax of` `HH77` EQUALS 1880
#ASSERT `CPF of` `HH77` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `net of` `HH77` EQUALS 58120

